posts.body:
MZ has built-in support for right-to-left display of text. By default the check is for Arabic characters:
Spoiler:
core snippets
JavaScript:
Utils.containsArabic = function(str) {
    const regExp = /[\u0600-\u06FF\u0750-\u077F\u08A0-\u08FF]/;
    return regExp.test(str);
};

Game_Message.prototype.isRTL = function() {
    return Utils.containsArabic(this.allText());
};

Window_Base.prototype.createTextState = function(text, x, y, width) {
    const rtl = Utils.containsArabic(text);
// ...
}
So I guess your text includes Arabic characters, maybe the hands?
If you don't care about supporting RTL text then a plugin like this might help (untested):
JavaScript:
/*:
 * @target MZ
 * @plugindesc Disable core support for right-to-left text.
 * @author Caethyril
 * @url https://forums.rpgmakerweb.com/threads/176594/
 * @help Free to use and/or modify for any project, no credit required.
 */
Utils.containsArabic = function() { return false; };
Alternatively you could look for similar characters, e.g. via a site like
https://shapecatcher.com/
.

